      en: "Maliana Valley is located in northwestern East Timor, in the Bobonaro district. The valley is drained by the Maliana River, which often floods during the rainy season, depositing fertile alluvial soils. The economy is based on intensive rice cultivation, often in terraces, and coffee plantations on the slopes. Local communities live in traditional mud-brick houses with palm-thatched roofs. The valley hosts endemic bird species and rare orchids. The valley floor lies at about 200 meters elevation, while surrounding mountains rise to 1000 meters.",
